{
  "answer": "You should use the `root_path` configuration to handle this case. This allows you to configure your application to use a specific path prefix, even if the proxy adds a prefix to the URL. \n\nFor example, you can declare a path at `/app` in your code, but then add a layer on top (the proxy) that puts your **FastAPI** application under a path like `/api/v1`. The `root_path` configuration will handle this case by stripping the path prefix on the fly before transmitting the request to the app server. \n\nThis way, your application will be convinced that it is being served at `/app`, and you don't have to update all your code to include the prefix `/api/v1`. \n\n[advanced/behind-a-proxy-6]",
